exit: 0

stdout:
warning[grice_rules/no-length-for-emptiness]: Length used to check for emptiness
   ┌─ src/app.gleam:11:8
   │
11 │   case string.length(name) == 0 {
   │        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This counts every grapheme of the string

`string.length` walks the whole string to count its graphemes, and its docs
say to avoid it in a loop. Comparing with `""` answers the same question at
once.

Hint: Compare with `""` instead: `== ""`.

warning[grice_rules/no-echo]: Leftover `echo`
   ┌─ src/app.gleam:13:14
   │
13 │     False -> echo "Hello, " <> name
   │              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This prints debug output when it runs

`echo` is for debugging. `gleam build` accepts it, but `gleam publish`
refuses a package that still has one, and an application prints it whenever
this code runs.

Hint: Remove the `echo` and keep its value: write `x` for `echo x`, and
drop an `echo` step from a pipeline. If this module prints on purpose, use
`gleam/io` instead.

2 warnings in 1 module.


